  "content": {
    "title": "Is Good Friday a federal holiday? Will mail get delivered? What to know before Easter 2026",
    "text": "April 3, 2026, 5:10 a.m. ETIf you’re planning to send out packages today, you’re in luck.Good Friday, a Christian religious observance, is not recognized as a federal holiday in the United States. That means many essential services, including mail delivery, continue operating as usual.Here’s a look at what’s open and closed on Good Friday from banks and the stock market to USPS mail delivery:Is Good Friday a federal holiday in the U.S.?Good Friday is not specified by law to be one of the 12 federal holidays recognized in 2026, according to opm.gov.Is USPS post office open on Good Friday? Will mail be delivered April 3, 2026?The United States Postal Service will be open, and mail will be delivered on Good Friday, April 3, 2026.Is FedEx open on Good Friday, April 3, 2026?FedEx and FedEx Freight will have modified service on Good Friday, April 3, 2026, but all other delivery options are expected to operate as normal.Is UPS open today on Good Friday, April 3, 2026?UPS Store is open and UPS delivery and pickup services are available on Good Friday, April 3, 2026.Is the stock market open on Good Friday, April 3, 2026? Is the stock market closed today?The stock markets on New York Stock Exchange and the Nasdaq are closed for trading on Good Friday, April 3, 2026. The Securities Industry and Financial Markets Association also recommended an early close at noon EST for the holiday.Will banks be closed on Good Friday, April 3, 2026? Are banks open today?Most banks will be open on Good Friday, April 3, 2026, according to The Federal Reserve.Is Good Friday a state holiday in Kentucky?Good Friday is a state holiday in Kentucky. State government offices will have a half-day.Are Kentucky schools closed today on Good Friday?Some schools may close on Good Friday, but several will remain open in the commonwealth. Be sure to check with your local school for details.Chris Sims is a trending reporter at Midwest Connect Gannett. Follow him on Twitter: @ChrisFSims. Reach Marina Johnson at Marina.Johnson@courier-journal.com.",
